WebCore: IntPoint::scaled() is not constexpr with GCC and libc++.

    IntPoint.h:88: error: call to non-'constexpr' function
        'long int std::__math::lround(float)'

IntPoint::scaled() is declared constexpr and calls std::lround().  libstdc++
lets GCC fold lround as a builtin; libc++ (the C++ library of QNX's GCC
toolchain) declares it as an ordinary function, and GCC 12 -- which predates
C++23's relaxed rule for constexpr functions (P2448) -- rejects a non-template
constexpr function whose body can never be a constant expression.  Nothing
uses scaled() in a constant expression, so drop the constexpr.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/IntPoint.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/IntPoint.h
@@ -83,12 +83,12 @@
         this->scale(scale, scale);
     }
 
-    constexpr IntPoint scaled(float scale) const
+    IntPoint scaled(float scale) const
     {
         return { static_cast<int>(std::lround(m_x * scale)), static_cast<int>(std::lround(m_y * scale)) };
     }
 
-    constexpr IntPoint scaled(float scaleX, float scaleY) const
+    IntPoint scaled(float scaleX, float scaleY) const
     {
         return { static_cast<int>(std::lround(m_x * scaleX)), static_cast<int>(std::lround(m_y * scaleY)) };
     }
